Z||000010||RaidenCobra||05-30-2001||05:08 AM||||Ok, I need some help asking this guy to test drive his car.. What should I tell him?<BR>Im going to need to borrow it for a few hours so I can drive down to london and meet up with PBJ. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Fierodave2001||05-30-2001||07:40 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by RaidenCobra:<BR><B>Ok, I need some help asking this guy to test drive his car.. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Just tell him straight out, I want my mechanic to look over the car & where he's located.  If he balks, then he's hiding something.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000012||Ken Wittlief||05-30-2001||10:27 AM||||NEVER!!! buy a car if you cant test drive it - unless you are buying a parts car!!!<P> Drive it on the highway up to 70mph, drive it down a bumpy road, drive it at least 10 miles - 15 to 20 minutes - make sure it reaches full operating temp.<P> When an owner wont let you drive a car that is licensed he is hiding something - accept no excuses.<P>  However - it is not reasonable to demand that he let you drive it alone - its normal for him to go along for the ride -letting you take the car for a 'few hours' is asking alot. There have been a lot of 17 year old kids that have totalled cars on 'test drives'.||||reg||1
